WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:07.630
Hi, I'm Lucy, 19 from Australia and How I Met Your Mother has been my favourite show for as long as I can remember.
嗨，我是露西，19岁，来自澳大利亚。《老爸老妈浪漫史》是我记事起最喜欢的节目。

2
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:13.510
Unfortunately, this weird phenomenon has started happening with the last three times I've re-watched the show I've been broken up with.
不幸的是，最近三次我重温这部剧时，都发生了这种诡异的现象：我被甩了。

3
00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.290
Nevertheless, I continue to watch all nine seasons during my morning period.
尽管如此，我还是在我的哀伤期里看完了全部九季。

4
00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:22.630
I told this to the last guy whilst he was breaking up with me and he asked why I don't just stop re-watching the show.
我在上一个男生跟我分手时把这事告诉了他，他问我为什么不干脆别再重温这部剧了。

5
00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:30.630
I told him how I believe that I have an instinct, that I'm about to go through something hard and subconsciously I turn to How I Met Your Mother
我告诉他，我相信自己有一种直觉，觉得我即将经历艰难的事情，于是潜意识里我转向了《老爸老妈浪漫史》，

6
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.510
because it brings me hope and comfort for the future and that the best is ahead of me.
因为它给我带来了对未来的希望和安慰，让我相信最好的时光还在前方。

7
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:41.510
So I want to thank you for creating this hilarious, complex show that I'm able to move past these hardships in my life.
所以我想感谢你们创作了这部搞笑而复杂的剧集，让我能够度过生活中的这些艰难困苦。

8
00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:50.250
I'm alone, we'll be soon, in New York City.
我孤身一人，很快就会在纽约市相聚。

9
00:00:51.330 --> 00:01:00.290
When I see you, please permit me to tell you everything, in New York City.
当我见到你时，请允许我在纽约市把一切都告诉你。

10
00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:03.990
Well, hello, welcome to another episode of How We Made Your Mother.
各位好，欢迎收看《我们是如何创造老爸老妈的》的又一期节目。

11
00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:04.610
I'm Josh Ratter.
我是乔什·拉特.

12
00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:05.950
I'm here with my friend Craig Thomas.
我和我的朋友克雷格·托马斯在一起。

13
00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:06.510
Hey, Craig.
嘿，克雷格。

14
00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:07.430
Hey, Josh.
嘿，乔什。

15
00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.570
Thank you, Lucy, for that great letter.
谢谢你，露西，谢谢你写来这封精彩的信。

16
00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:17.570
I would like to remind you, I think that there's a phenomenon in our brain, it always thinks we're at the end of our story.
我想提醒你，我认为我们的大脑中存在一种现象，它总是认为我们正处于故事的结尾。

17
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:23.710
And it was great to hear that you were 19 years old and so self-possessed and you had so much wisdom.
听到你才19岁就如此自信、拥有如此多的智慧，这真是太棒了。

18
00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.750
And, you know, Ted thought his story was over at 27, but it was just beginning.
而且，你知道，泰德以为他的故事在27岁时就结束了，但那其实只是开始。

19
00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:29.290
That's right.
没错。

20
00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:33.490
And I love that she gets a feeling like something is going to happen in the universe.
我喜欢她有一种感觉，觉得宇宙中将要发生什么。

21
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.290
There's like an intuition and then she's like, I need to watch How I Met Your Mother.
就像有一种直觉，然后她就会想：我得看看《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

22
00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.370
That's amazing.
太神奇了。

23
00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.490
I love that the show's got comfort to her, but it also, there's a slight ominousness.
我很高兴这部剧能给她带来安慰，但同时，这也带有一丝不祥的预兆。

24
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.250
Like, is How I Met Your Mother causing these problems in her life?
比如，是《老爸老妈浪漫史》导致了她生活中的这些问题吗？

25
00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:44.650
I don't know.
我不知道。

26
00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:45.150
I hope not.
但愿不是。

27
00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.610
Do you have a reaction when you hear the theme song?
当你听到主题曲时，你会有什么反应吗？

28
00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.370
Does it trigger something?
它会触发什么回忆吗？

29
00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:54.290
Well, we're so happy that we could be there for you in your tough times, in your joyous times.
嗯，我们很高兴能在你艰难的时刻、快乐的时刻陪伴着你。

30
00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.790
Deep into season four here today, we're talking about episode five.
今天我们深入探讨第四季，聊聊第五集。

31
00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:02.030
It's called Shelter Island.
它叫《避难所岛》。

32
00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.690
Remind me who wrote this episode, Craig.
提醒我一下这一集是谁写的，克雷格。

33
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.750
Chris Harris, the great Chris Harris.
克里斯·哈里斯，伟大的克里斯·哈里斯。

34
00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:06.570
Ah, Chris Harris.
啊，克里斯·哈里斯。

35
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:13.470
I met a psychologist this weekend, Laurie Gottlieb, who is a great writer and psychologiSt.
我这周末遇到了一位心理学家，洛瑞·戈特利布，她是一位优秀的作家兼心理学家。

36
00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:14.890
And she said, do you know Chris Harris?
她说，你认识克里斯·哈里斯吗？

37
00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:15.870
Everyone knows Chris Harris.
谁不认识克里斯·哈里斯啊。

38
00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:17.150
She went to school with Hillary.
她和希拉里一起上过学。

39
00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:18.170
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

40
00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:18.930
And has known them a long time.
而且认识他们很久了。

41
00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.710
Chris's lovely wife, Hillary Lipton, also a really good writer.
克里斯可爱的妻子希拉里·利普顿，也是一位非常优秀的作家。

42
00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.510
Alec, remind us when this episode aired?
亚历克，提醒我们这集是什么时候播出的？

43
00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:27.670
Originally on October 20th, 2008.
最初于2008年10月20日播出。

44
00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:29.510
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

45
00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:30.810
That's a minute ago.
那是好一会儿以前了。

46
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:31.330
18-hoo.
18岁呜呼。

47
00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.890
And who is that woo-hooing?
刚才那是谁在呜呼？

48
00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.150
Do we think we should get to that?
我们觉得该进入正题了吗？

49
00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.630
I thought that was a guest woo-hoo.
我以为那是嘉宾的欢呼。

50
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:41.390
But do you want to give us a woo-hoo to announce yourself?
但你想自我介绍似地来一声欢呼吗？

51
00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.970
I was told to be silent until spoken to.
我被告知在被点名之前要保持安静。

52
00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.790
So you can't get above a certain octave.
所以你的音高不能超过某个八度。

53
00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:47.330
Correct.
没错。

54
00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:48.350
We limited that.
我们限制了这一点。

55
00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:49.070
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

56
00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:49.650
There it is.
就是这样。

57
00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:49.970
Close.
接近了。

58
00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.930
Now I want to hear that blur sound.
现在我想听听那个模糊的声音。

59
00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.610
Craig, introduce our very special gueSt.
克雷格，介绍一下我们的特邀嘉宾。

60
00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.930
We have the great Jason Jones with us, ladies and gentlemen.
女士们先生们，我们请来了伟大的杰森·琼斯。

61
00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:58.630
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

62
00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.710
Now we give him a woo-hoo back.
现在我们回敬他一声呜呼。

63
00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:00.170
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

64
00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:04.830
Who is excellent in this episode, which is also just an excellent episode.
他在这一集里表现极佳，而且这一集本身也极为精彩。

65
00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:08.730
I started to say before we were going to record how I hadn't seen this episode.
在开始录制之前，我正想说我还没看过这一集。

66
00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:09.410
And it was great.
而且它真的很棒。

67
00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:12.550
And then I got cut off by everyone because everything has to be content.
然后我被所有人打断了，因为一切都必须是内容。

68
00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:13.730
Everything has to be monetized.
一切都必须商业化。

69
00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.130
I can't say words unless we're selling ad time.
除非我们在卖广告时间，否则我都不能说话。

70
00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:20.750
But what I was going to say before you guys told me to shut up is I loved this one so much.
但正如你们叫我闭嘴之前我想说的那样，我太喜欢这一集了。

71
00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:24.730
I really had not seen this in 18 years, you know, since it aired maybe.
我真的有18年没看过这个了，你知道的，大概自从它播出以来。

72
00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:28.570
And I, this to me is like one of the greats.
对我来说，这简直是神作之一。

73
00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.330
This is one of the great How Much Mother episodes.
这是《老爸老妈浪漫史》中最棒的剧集之一。

74
00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.350
It's so dark and weird and unexpected.
它是如此黑暗、诡异且出人意料。

75
00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.470
And you're so hilarious in it, Jason.
你在里面太搞笑了，杰森。

76
00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:39.350
But it also like, you're so funny in the sort of A side of the episode that at the very end,
但同时，你在这一集的A线里表现得如此好笑，以至于到了最后，

77
00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:43.070
the reveal is much more shocking because of how funny.
因为之前那么好笑，最后的揭秘才显得更加震撼。

78
00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:43.850
You're so funny.
你太搞笑了。

79
00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.350
But then it gets very, very real in a way that like it really threw.
但随后它变得非常非常真实，甚至有点让人措手不及。

80
00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:51.250
I felt surprised by what happened in an episode of TV I worked on.
我竟然会对一部我参与制作的电视剧的发展感到惊讶。

81
00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:51.890
So that was well done.
所以这真的很了不起。

82
00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.550
Well, why don't you, Craig, before we go in a little deeper,
那么，克雷格，在我们深入探讨之前，

83
00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:57.130
why don't you tell us, just give us your armchair summary of what happens in this episode
你为什么不给我们大概讲讲这一集发生了什么，

84
00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:57.950
to just orient us.
好让我们有个概念。

85
00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.150
This is the episode where Ted gets.
这就是泰德被……的那一集。

86
00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.850
Honestly, I'm going to need that as well.
说实话，我也需要有人提醒一下。

87
00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:01.530
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

88
00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.350
Here's, Jason, I'm going to tell you what you did in the episode before he complimented you.
这样吧，杰森，在他夸你之前，我来告诉你你在这一集里干了什么。

89
00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:06.370
What show is this again?
这到底是哪个节目来着？

90
00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:07.610
This is The Daily Show.
这是《每日秀》。

91
00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:08.770
This is the one where you went.
这就是你去了的那集。

92
00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:09.310
Got it, got it, got it.
懂了，懂了，懂了。

93
00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.550
No, so this is the episode where Ted gets left at the altar.
好吧，这就是泰德在婚礼上被放鸽子的那一集。

94
00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:16.650
That's, I mean, if you had to distill it down to one knockout punch, that's it.
我是说，如果你非要把它浓缩成最核心的一点，就是这个。

95
00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:21.530
But it has this great storytelling device of kids never bring an ex,
但它有一个很棒的叙事手法，就是孩子们千万别带前任，

96
00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:23.210
never invite an ex to your wedding.
千万别邀请前任参加你的婚礼。

97
00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:27.470
And it is very much steered towards, oh, my God, Ted invited Robin to the wedding.
而且它一直在往这个方向引导：天哪，泰德竟然邀请了罗宾参加婚礼。

98
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:28.610
What's going to happen?
会发生什么呢？

99
00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.210
At the very end, you realize Robin was not actually,
到了最后你会发现，罗宾其实并不是，

100
00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:35.530
Robin was a red herring and there was a whole other thing in this story.
罗宾只是个烟雾弹，故事里其实还有完全不同的另一条线。

101
00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.090
And that thing is, Stella winds up deciding to go back with her ex,
而且那件事就是，斯特拉最后决定和她的前男友复合，

102
00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:40.750
Tony, played by the great Jason Jones.
托尼，由伟大的杰森·琼斯饰演。

103
00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:44.830
And it's just, there's a lot in 22 minutes, don't you think?
而且怎么说呢，22分钟里塞了太多内容了，你不觉得吗？

104
00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.370
This felt like a two-parter.
这感觉像是一集上下集的故事。

105
00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:47.370
It's definitely plot heavy.
剧情绝对非常饱满。

106
00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.130
Yeah, I loved it.
对，我超喜欢。

107
00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:48.970
It's very plot heavy.
剧情真的很满。

108
00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:52.670
You know, it's also like, never invite an ex to a wedding.
你知道的，这就好比，千万别邀请前任去婚礼。

109
00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:57.550
Sometimes the narrator says things a little bit like, well, this is probably, this is a suggestion.
有时旁白会说一些这样的话，嗯，这大概是，这是一个建议。

110
00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.530
Nothing good happens after 2 a.m.
凌晨两点后没有好事发生

111
00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.710
and never invite an ex to a wedding are so, he's so certain that those are.
和千万别邀请前任去婚礼是如此地，他确信那些是。

112
00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.030
Future Ted meant that shit.
未来的泰德是认真的。

113
00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.310
He really meant that.
他是真的很认真。

114
00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:07.130
Iron clad advice.
铁律一般的忠告。

115
00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.450
Never invite an ex to a wedding.
千万别邀请前任去婚礼。

116
00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:15.770
Jason, I mean, it's been, I hate to say this, it's been 18 years since we filmed this episode.
杰森，我的意思是，天呐，我不愿承认，距离我们拍摄这一集已经过去18年了。

117
00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:17.370
It's been a long, that's a long time.
这真的是，太久了。

118
00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:18.030
That shocked me.
这把我惊到了。

119
00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:18.110
A long time.
好久啊。

120
00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:23.150
You were like, I would have said like 2012, 13 is when I was thinking it was, but 2008.
你当时就说，我本来会猜大概是2012、2013年左右，但居然是2008年。

121
00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:23.810
I know.
我知道。

122
00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:24.410
It's rough.
太残忍了。

123
00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.290
Do you, what are your memories of shooting this?
你，你对拍摄这一集还有什么记忆吗？

124
00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:29.690
I mean, you did a couple episodes, right?
我的意思是，你演了好几集，对吧？

125
00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:30.430
Yeah, you did.
对，你演了。

126
00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:30.750
I think so, yeah.
我想是的，没错。

127
00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.070
You did several with us.
你和我们合作了好几集。

128
00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:36.970
You appear very briefly in the one after this, but then at the end of the season, you
你在紧接着的那一集里短暂露面，但后来在季末的时候，你

129
00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:41.170
had, there's a very big episode featuring your character, Tony, who has this huge impact
有了一集非常重磅的戏份，你的角色托尼对泰德的生活

130
00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:41.890
on Ted's life.
产生了巨大的影响。

131
00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:46.170
Like future Ted is able to say, I never would have become a professor at Columbia if it weren't
就像未来的泰德可以说，如果不是这家伙因为我被抛弃在婚礼上而对我感到内疚，

132
00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:49.630
for this guy feeling bad for me because of what happened getting left at the altar.
我绝不可能成为哥伦比亚大学的教授。

133
00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:54.010
So Tony, your character actually plays a really pivotal role in Ted's life.
所以托尼，你的角色其实在泰德的人生中扮演了非常关键的角色。

134
00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:56.110
And so you do come back later in the season in a big way.
所以你在本季后半段确实以极其重要的戏份回归了。

135
00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:58.130
And there was another one too.
还有另外一集。

136
00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.750
And like the next season too, wasn't it?
好像下一季也有，对吧？

137
00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.670
I just remember eating at a dinner table.
我只记得我在餐桌旁吃东西。

138
00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:02.810
Yeah.
对。

139
00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:03.110
Yeah.
对。

140
00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.510
I didn't have any lines.
我一句台词也没有。

141
00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:05.830
I was just like eating steak.
我当时就在那儿狂吃牛排。

142
00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:06.590
Yeah.
对。

143
