00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:18.440
True stories.
真实的故事。

294
00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:19.920
No holding back.
毫无保留。

295
00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:22.720
He comes up behind me and whispers right in my ear.
他走到我身后，在我耳边低语。

296
00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:30.010
These stories will make you laugh till you're crying.
这些故事会让你笑到流泪。

297
00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.970
And then I realize I'm unconscious.
然后我才意识到我已经失去知觉了。

298
00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.510
Some will stick with you for life.
有些故事会让你铭记一生。

299
00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.470
They catch my mom poisoning my sister.
他们撞见我母亲在毒害我姐姐。

300
00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:42.170
My brother, he died at the hands of my mother.
我弟弟，他死在我母亲的手里。

301
00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:44.030
I said, Mike, don't make me shoot you, please.
我说，迈克，别逼我开枪射你，求你了。

302
00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:45.090
But he did.
但他还是开了枪。

303
00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:22.010
And now, back's the show.
好了，现在回到节目。

304
00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:31.650
Jason, that first scene between us when I come to your apartment and I walked, when I saw myself walking, I said to my wife, Jordana, who's never seen the show.
杰森，我们之间的第一场戏，就是我去你公寓的那场，当我看到自己走路的样子时，我对我的妻子乔达娜说——她从来没看过这个节目——

305
00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:32.510
That's part of what we're doing.
这就是我们正在做的事情的一部分。

306
00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:36.410
It's like, I'm showing her the show for the first time, which is a fun thing.
这就好比，我第一次把这个节目放给她看，这挺有意思的。

307
00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:39.230
But I remember saying to her, this is a good scene.
但我记得当时对她说，这是一场好戏。

308
00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:42.890
And for some reason, I watched certain scenes and I have no memory of shooting them.
而且不知为什么，我看某些场景时，完全不记得当时拍过它们。

309
00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:45.310
And other scenes are seared into my imagination.
而另一些场景则深深烙印在我的脑海里。

310
00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:47.150
That's like, I remember that day.
就像是，我记得那一天。

311
00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:48.290
I remember that scene.
我记得那一场戏。

312
00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:49.970
I remember the feel of doing it.
我记得当时表演时的感觉。

313
00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:56.850
And this scene between Ted and Tony is one of those scenes that I knew while we were doing it, it was a good scene.
泰德和托尼之间的这场戏就是那种场景，我们在拍的时候我就知道，这是一场好戏。

314
00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:57.670
Do you have that?
你有过这种感觉吗？

315
00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:58.750
Did you have that memory?
你有过那样的记忆吗？

316
00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:00.090
Like, I just knew it was working.
比如说，我当时就觉得它效果很好。

317
00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:01.210
Yeah.
对。

318
00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:05.590
I'm not sure when it works, but I'm always sure when it doesn't work.
我不确定什么时候它能成功，但我总是很清楚什么时候它会失败。

319
00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.650
And it wasn't working.
而当时效果并不好。

320
00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:09.030
Yeah.
对。

321
00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:09.970
It wasn't working.
当时效果确实不好。

322
00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:10.390
Yeah.
对。

323
00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:14.630
Like, it's just, it's one of those things I'm like, this is not good.
就像，这正是那种让我觉得“这可不太妙”的事情。

324
00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:15.410
This is not good.
这太糟糕了。

325
00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:16.430
And it didn't feel that way to me.
但我自己并没有这种感觉。

326
00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:18.670
So whether or not that means it works, I don't know.
所以这是否意味着它管用，我也不知道。

327
00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:22.750
Were you thrown by, I mean, had you done multi-camera sitcoms like with an audience?
你有没有被……我是说，你以前演过带现场观众的多机位情景喜剧吗？

328
00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:28.950
I had done one pilot with a live audience, which I did not like.
我拍过一个带现场观众的试播集，我其实不太喜欢。

329
00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:30.390
I liked the pilot.
我挺喜欢那个试播集的。

330
00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:34.210
The pilot was great, but performing in front of a live audience was not my thing.
试播集很棒，但在现场观众面前表演不是我的风格。

331
00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:40.130
So did you appreciate kind of doing the form of a live multi-camp sitcom without the audience there?
那你是不是挺欣赏这种没有现场观众的多机位情景喜剧形式的？

332
00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.810
It was listening to Michael Shea's laughter that threw me off.
是迈克尔·谢伊的笑声把我弄糊涂了。

333
00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:47.610
And the crew laughs once, generally at rehearsal, and then you're on your own.
剧组通常在排练时会笑一次，然后你就得靠自己了。

334
00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:49.350
You got to build in the laughter.
你必须在表演中留出笑声的空间。

335
00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:49.870
That's right.
没错。

336
00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:50.250
That's right.
对的。

337
00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:54.510
So that's always a little weird, finding something to do while Michael Shea laughs for you.
所以这总是有点怪怪的，当迈克尔·谢伊为你发笑时，你还得找点事做。

338
00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:58.550
We just had him on an episode, and we were...
我们刚刚请他上了一期节目，然后我们……

339
00:14:58.550 --> 00:14:59.010
He's great.
他太棒了。

340
00:14:59.170 --> 00:14:59.630
He's amazing.
他了不起。

341
00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:00.810
Such a great guy.
真是个好人。

342
00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:01.450
And Pam, too.
还有帕姆也是。

343
00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:03.870
Pam's a wonderful, wonderful human being, obviously.
帕姆显然是个非常非常棒的人。

344
00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:04.830
You guys know that.
你们大家也都知道。

345
00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:11.570
But yeah, it was an adjustment period, but not a long one, you know?
不过是的，这有一段适应期，但并不长，你知道吗？

346
00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:12.790
Again, I'm an actor.
再说一次，我是一名演员。

347
00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:13.830
You fit right in.
你完全融入进去了。

348
00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.050
You fit in so well.
你融入得太完美了。

349
00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:20.110
And it's an interesting line to walk of like, you are the comic relief in this episode.
而且这是一个很有趣的平衡点，就像，你是这集里的喜剧担当。

350
00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:21.430
Tony is a ridiculous character.
托尼是个荒诞的角色。

351
00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:24.210
He doesn't want to allow his daughter to go to this wedding.
他不想让女儿去参加这个婚礼。

352
00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:24.710
Right.
对。

353
00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:31.150
And you have to play it as sort of like a crazy alpha male buffoon who then sort of collapses,
你得把它演成那种疯狂的大男子主义滑稽丑角，然后突然崩溃，

354
00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:33.830
and you see immediately that he's just very hurt.
然后你马上能看出其实他只是深受伤害。

355
00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:35.370
And then he's very lovable.
而且接下来他非常惹人喜爱。

356
00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:41.310
But he also has to somehow, you have to at the end buy that Stella chooses him over Ted.
但同时他又必须，你得让观众在最后相信斯特拉选择了托尼而不是泰德。

357
00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:45.850
And I think you played it with like, just the right amount of comedy on the A side.
我觉得你把喜剧效果拿捏得恰到好处，前半部分分寸刚刚好。

358
00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:52.550
And just there were these little scenes you had to do with Sarah Chalk where we had to see you guys like, together.
而且你和莎拉·乔克有一些必须演的小对手戏，我们得看到你们俩在一起的样子。

359
00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:55.770
It had you, there were these little moments of connection that worked.
这里有那些彼此连接的小瞬间，而且效果很好。

360
00:15:56.010 --> 00:16:01.750
And like, really, at that end of that episode, it's like, oh shit, Tony totally stole Stella back from Ted.
而且真的，在那集快结束的时候，会觉得，靠，托尼居然把斯特拉从泰德身边抢回来了。

361
00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:07.770
Like, that happened, and I bought it, and I thought it was expertly done how you had both of those energies in this episode.
没错，事情就这样发生了，而且我很买账，我觉得你在这集里把这两种气场都处理得妙到毫巅。

362
00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:08.330
So, well done.
所以，干得漂亮。

363
00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:15.410
Well, that might have been on you guys, because I feel like the first scene that I shot was on the ferry.
好吧，那也许得归功于你们，因为我觉得我拍的第一场戏是在渡轮上。

364
00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:16.790
Is that the first up?
那是第一场吗？

365
00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.170
Making out with Sarah.
和莎拉舌吻。

366
00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:19.670
Well, that was terrible planning.
好吧，那真是糟糕的计划。

367
00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:20.430
Michael Shea.
迈克尔·谢伊。

368
00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:21.330
Hey, just kiss.
嘿，直接亲。

369
00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:21.970
Just kiss.
直接亲。

370
00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:23.230
You guys make out for a bit.
你们俩亲热一会儿。

371
00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:26.250
And then I'm like, all right, I guess we're, I guess we're in love.
然后我就想，好吧，我想我们，我想我们恋爱了。

372
00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:28.450
So, we sort of backtracked after that.
所以之后我们有点像是倒着拍的。

373
00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:31.290
I'm like, once you make out, you know, we got some, we got some sort of connection.
我想，一旦你们亲过了，你知道的，我们就建立某种联系了。

374
00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:32.890
And we're both Canadian.
而且我们都是加拿大人。

375
00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.310
That was a connection, you know.
这也是一种联系，你知道的。

376
00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:35.230
You're both Canadian.
你们俩都是加拿大人。

377
00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:36.010
That's right.
没错。

378
00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:36.410
Yeah.
对。

379
00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:36.890
That's right.
没错。

380
00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:40.210
Well, you guys, there was something I bought about that in this big way.
总之，你们俩之间那种感觉让我深信不疑。

381
00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:45.550
And I, like, in 22 minutes, Tony went from this buffoon to, like, this is the greatest moment of Tony's life.
而且我觉得，在22分钟里，托尼从一个丑角变成了——就像这是托尼人生中最棒的时刻。

382
00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:46.890
He has achieved this.
他做到了。

383
00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:51.290
And the ending is very sad and very dark and a real surprise.
而且结局非常悲伤、非常黑暗，真的让人感到意外。

384
00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:53.510
Like, I really felt like the surprise worked.
我觉得这种反转效果真的很棒。

385
00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:58.110
And I think it's a testament to you, because you're so funny, but I think you do have, you have charisma.
我觉得这要归功于你，因为你不仅非常搞笑，而且你确实很有个人魅力。

386
00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:03.390
Like, there's something about it where you're like, in the end, I like this guy, Tony, and I buy that she would go with him.
就那种感觉，到最后你会觉得，我喜欢托尼这个家伙，而且我相信她会跟他走。

387
00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:05.830
Again, I'm going to chuck that up to acting.
话又说回来，我把这归功于演技。

388
00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:07.370
I have no charisma in real life.
我在现实生活中毫无魅力。

389
00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:12.210
And you began more acting acting than comedy acting.
你一开始是做正剧表演多过喜剧表演吗？

390
00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:12.770
Is that right?
是这样吗？

391
00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:13.850
Or am I misremembering that?
还是我记错了？

392
00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:14.150
I did.
是的。

393
00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:17.090
I thought I was going to do Shakespeare for the rest of my life.
我本以为我这辈子都要演莎士比亚了。

394
00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:23.650
I went to a fairly dramatic theater school that was sort of specialized in that.
我进了一所相当注重正剧的戏剧学校，那里的教学比较偏向这个。

395
00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:28.710
And I got on a touring Shakespeare show, and about a month into it, I was like, this sucks.
后来我加入了一个莎士比亚巡演剧团，大概演了一个月，我就觉得，这太烂了。

396
00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:34.850
This sucks doing this, like, every single night to people who don't really want to watch it.
每天晚上都这样演给那些其实根本不想看的人听，这太烂了。

397
00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:36.950
They're just there because they feel like it's important.
他们来只是因为觉得这很重要。

398
00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:44.670
And I walked into a bar one night, and there was, like, in the back room, they were doing sketch comedy with a buddy.
有一天晚上我走进一家酒吧，后面房间里有个朋友在表演素描喜剧。

399
00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.410
And we both looked at him, and we were like, well, we could do this better.
我们俩看着他，心里都在想，切，我们能比这演得更好。

400
00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.030
And that's just kind of how we started doing it.
我们就是这样开始干这个的。

401
00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:52.090
We're just like, look, we can beat this.
我们当时就想，看吧，我们能战胜这个。

402
00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.970
This wouldn't be the same thing every night.
这不会每晚都是同一个内容。

403
00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:55.050
We can change this.
我们可以改变这一点。

404
00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:56.710
Yeah, we can change it every single night.
对，我们可以每晚都改变它。

405
00:17:56.870 --> 00:18:02.110
And I remember when we got a manager, they were like, you guys keep changing the sketches.
我记得当我们请了经纪人时，他们说，你们怎么一直在改小品。

406
00:18:02.250 --> 00:18:02.870
Play your hits.
演你们的成名作吧。

407
00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:03.950
I'm like, I don't want to do that.
我说，我才不想那样。

408
00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:05.110
I want to change it every night.
我想每天晚上都做出改变。

409
00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.290
I want to do something new every single time.
我希望每次都做点新鲜的。

410
00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:11.590
That's what excited me, not, like, playing a sketch that worked once or twice.
这才是让我兴奋的事，而不是去演那些成功过一两次的小品。

411
00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:12.050
Yeah.
对。

412
00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:16.130
One of my favorite stories, I might have shared this on the pod before, Craig,
我最喜欢的几个故事之一，我可能以前在播客里分享过，克雷格，

413
00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:21.530
but in Patti Smith's memoir, Just Kids, she was a poet and a photographer.
但在帕蒂·史密斯的自传《只是孩子》里，她曾是个诗人和摄影师。

414
00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:22.890
Living in New York.
住在纽约。

415
00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.770
And she went and saw Iggy Pop play one time.
有一次她去看伊基·波普的演出。

416
00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:27.430
He was thrashing around on stage.
他在舞台上疯狂地扭动甩打。

417
00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:30.810
And something in her, this voice in her head went, I can do that.
她体内的某种东西，脑海中的一个声音说，我能做到那个。

418
00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:31.770
Right.
没错。

419
00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:32.770
She was like, I can do that.
她心想，我能做到那样。

420
00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:37.270
And she just became a rock star because she was like, she had this certainty, like, I can
她就那样成了一名摇滚巨星，因为她当时坚信，就像，我能

421
00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:37.590
do that.
做到。

422
00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:42.250
And I feel like there are those moments where you watch someone and something in you takes
我觉得总会有那么一些时刻，当你看着某个人时，你体内的某种东西被唤醒了

423
00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:45.130
over, like some deeper, wiser part of you that's like, this is for you.
就像你内心某个更深沉、更睿智的部分在说，这正是为你准备的。

424
00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:45.890
You can do this.
你能做到这一点。

425
00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:46.910
I saw Iggy Pop live once.
我现场看过伊基·波普的演出。

426
00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:48.510
I did not have that same thought.
我可没有产生那种想法。

427
00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:52.370
You're like, I smear myself in peanut butter, but for other reasons.
你大概会想，我把自己涂满花生酱，但那是出于其他原因。

428
00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:53.510
That's amazing.
太棒了。

429
00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.150
I did a movie with Iggy Pop.
我和伊基·波普拍过一部电影。

430
00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:55.590
No.
不会吧。

431
00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:56.090
What?
什么？

432
00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:57.050
And wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等。

433
00:18:57.270 --> 00:18:59.350
And here's the connection to this podcaSt.
接下来就是和本播客的联系了。

434
00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:01.330
Bob Saget was also in the movie.
鲍勃·萨吉特也参演了那部电影。

435
00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:02.190
This is insane.
这太疯狂了。

436
00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:03.710
It was Bob's last movie that he did.
那是鲍勃生前拍的最后一部电影。

437
00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:04.210
Oh my God.
噢天哪。

438
00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:05.890
So it wasn't even that long ago.
所以其实没过多久。

439
00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:06.490
No, no, no, no.
