887
00:36:40.190 --> 00:36:40.550
No.
没有。

888
00:36:42.030 --> 00:36:44.710
It's a magical place on Earth.
那是地球上一个神奇的地方。

889
00:36:44.710 --> 00:36:49.150
I went there briefly with kids and didn't do any hiking or exploring or anything real.
我以前带着孩子短暂去过那儿，根本没怎么徒步、探索，也没做什么实质性的事。

890
00:36:49.290 --> 00:36:50.850
I was briefly there, but not really there.
我在那儿待过一会儿，但没真正去体验。

891
00:36:51.290 --> 00:36:52.410
One of my kids was sick.
我的一个孩子生病了。

892
00:36:52.650 --> 00:36:53.510
It's incredible.
那地方太不可思议了。

893
00:36:53.750 --> 00:36:54.630
I really got no sense in it.
我真的没能好好体会。

894
00:36:54.650 --> 00:36:55.090
It's such an incredible place.
那是个太不可思议的地方了。

895
00:36:55.270 --> 00:37:00.590
So I climbed this thing called Half Dome, which is the North Face logo.
所以我爬了那个叫半圆顶的山，就是北面户外品牌的那个标志。

896
00:37:00.970 --> 00:37:01.210
Yeah.
对。

897
00:37:01.470 --> 00:37:02.370
Yes, that's it.
对，就是那个。

898
00:37:02.470 --> 00:37:03.190
That's Half Dome, yeah.
那是半圆顶，对。

899
00:37:03.710 --> 00:37:04.150
So we've seen it.
所以我们都见过。

900
00:37:04.330 --> 00:37:07.030
So the one side is there's a straight face, which is awful.
其中一面是垂直的峭壁，非常可怕。

901
00:37:07.290 --> 00:37:09.970
And then so the backside is easy, but it's not that easy.
所以背面其实挺容易的，但其实也没那么简单。

902
00:37:10.070 --> 00:37:11.950
Anyway, I'm going up these cables.
总之，我正顺着这些钢缆往上爬。

903
00:37:12.010 --> 00:37:12.630
I get up to the top.
我终于爬到了山顶。

904
00:37:12.630 --> 00:37:14.790
I was one of the only hiked fasts that was up there.
我是当时少数几个爬得很快并到达山顶的人之一。

905
00:37:15.010 --> 00:37:19.350
And as I'm coming down, there's this couple coming up, and they look up at me, and they're like,
当我往下走的时候，有一对情侣正往上走，他们抬头看着我，然后说：

906
00:37:20.850 --> 00:37:21.630
How I Met Your Mother.
《老爸老妈的浪漫史》。

907
00:37:22.030 --> 00:37:22.850
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

908
00:37:22.970 --> 00:37:29.750
I'm like, don't we want to get to the top first before you talk about that show?
我说，难道我们不应该先爬到山顶，再讨论那部剧吗？

909
00:37:29.890 --> 00:37:32.010
And they're like, it's our favorite show.
他们说，那是我们最喜欢的剧。

910
00:37:32.170 --> 00:37:33.390
It is our favorite show.
那是我们最喜欢的剧。

911
00:37:33.750 --> 00:37:34.150
Wow.
哇。

912
00:37:34.470 --> 00:37:34.650
Yeah.
是啊。

913
00:37:35.130 --> 00:37:37.610
That's a really cool place to be recognized.
能在那种地方被认出来真的很酷。

914
00:37:37.750 --> 00:37:39.530
And how did they have that at their fingertips?
而且他们怎么能张口就来呢？

915
00:37:39.730 --> 00:37:40.850
You're hiking, you're sweaty.
你在爬山，满身是汗。

916
00:37:41.130 --> 00:37:42.150
That was last week.
那是上周的事。

917
00:37:42.150 --> 00:37:43.990
This is 18 years on.
这已经是18年后的事了。

918
00:37:44.830 --> 00:37:46.370
Clearly, you still look pretty good, man.
显然，你看起来还是挺不错的，老兄。

919
00:37:46.570 --> 00:37:47.270
You still got it.
你宝刀未老啊。

920
00:37:47.470 --> 00:37:47.730
I guess.
大概吧。

921
00:37:47.730 --> 00:37:51.670
The weird thing, though, is, Jason, the people who are watching it and re-watching it all the time,
不过奇怪的是，杰森，那些一直在看、反复重温这部剧的人，

922
00:37:51.830 --> 00:37:53.850
they just saw that episode last week.
他们上周才刚刚看过那一集。

923
00:37:54.030 --> 00:37:54.390
That's true.
确实如此。

924
00:37:54.390 --> 00:37:55.130
That wasn't 18 years ago.
那可不是18年前拍的。

925
00:37:55.170 --> 00:37:56.470
It's not 18 years ago to them.
对他们来说，那不是18年前的事。

926
00:37:56.590 --> 00:37:56.670
Yeah.
是啊。

927
00:37:56.870 --> 00:37:57.330
That's right.
没错。

928
00:37:58.770 --> 00:38:08.510
Second thing, I was in this winery in Tuscany, and this woman was, like, staring at me the whole time.
第二件事，我在托斯卡纳的一家酒庄里，有个女人一直在盯着我看。

929
00:38:08.510 --> 00:38:09.630
She was leading the tour.
她是导游。

930
00:38:09.750 --> 00:38:10.750
She's like, I know you.
她说，我认识你。

931
00:38:10.810 --> 00:38:11.230
I know you.
我认识你。

932
00:38:11.490 --> 00:38:16.830
And then we're doing the wine sampling at the end, and she's like, Tony.
然后我们在最后品酒的时候，她突然说，托尼。

933
00:38:18.850 --> 00:38:19.470
I'm like, what?
我说，什么？

934
00:38:19.670 --> 00:38:20.270
No, it's Jason.
不对，我是杰森。

935
00:38:20.470 --> 00:38:22.590
She's like, Tony, from How I Met Your Mother.
她说，托尼，《老爸老妈的浪漫史》里的。

936
00:38:22.770 --> 00:38:23.730
It's my favorite shot.
这是我最喜欢的镜头。

937
00:38:23.730 --> 00:38:24.990
It took you a second to remember.
你花了一会儿才想起来。

938
00:38:25.190 --> 00:38:25.670
That's right.
没错。

939
00:38:25.770 --> 00:38:26.430
That was the character.
那是那个角色的名字。

940
00:38:26.590 --> 00:38:29.910
And then she's like, please, we have a lamp that celebrities sign.
然后她说，求你了，我们有一个专门让名人签名的台灯。

941
00:38:30.010 --> 00:38:30.610
Can you sign the lamp?
你能在这盏灯上签个名吗？

942
00:38:30.610 --> 00:38:33.690
I'm like, I don't consider myself a celebrity, but yeah.
我说，我不觉得自己是个名人，不过好吧。

943
00:38:33.890 --> 00:38:35.730
Well, I'm like six wines in.
当时我已经喝了大约六杯葡萄酒了。

944
00:38:35.810 --> 00:38:36.650
I'm like, I'll sign your lamp.
我说，我来给你的台灯签名。

945
00:38:36.710 --> 00:38:40.990
She's like, we only have one person signed so far, so you'd be number two.
她说，目前我们只收集到一个人的签名，所以你是第二个。

946
00:38:41.430 --> 00:38:48.090
And I swear to God, I swear to God, the other signature on the lamp, the Pope.
我发誓，我发誓，台灯上的另一个签名是，教皇。

947
00:38:50.490 --> 00:38:52.490
The Pope and Jason Jones.
教皇和杰森·琼斯。

948
00:38:52.610 --> 00:38:53.050
The Pope and me.
教皇和我。

949
00:38:53.230 --> 00:38:53.630
That was it.
就这两个人。

950
00:38:53.670 --> 00:38:55.350
On the celebrity lamp in Tuscany.
在托斯卡纳的名人台灯上。

951
00:38:55.570 --> 00:38:55.790
Yeah.
是啊。

952
00:38:56.110 --> 00:38:56.210
Yeah.
对。

953
00:38:56.490 --> 00:39:00.050
Dude, that is, you were signature number two?
老兄，那是，你是第二个签名的吗？

954
00:39:00.050 --> 00:39:01.890
I was signature number two.
我是第二个签名的。

955
00:39:01.990 --> 00:39:03.370
Well, now it's a celebrity lamp.
好吧，现在它是一盏名人台灯了。

956
00:39:03.550 --> 00:39:04.450
It didn't used to be.
以前可不是。

957
00:39:04.630 --> 00:39:05.330
Oh my God.
天哪。

958
00:39:05.650 --> 00:39:06.870
It was just a holy lamp.
它原本只是一盏神圣的台灯。

959
00:39:06.970 --> 00:39:07.690
It was a holy lamp.
它是一盏神圣的台灯。

960
00:39:07.690 --> 00:39:08.150
It was a holy lamp?
它是一盏神圣的台灯？

961
00:39:08.410 --> 00:39:09.490
No, it's a celebrity lamp.
不，这是一盏名人台灯。

962
00:39:09.710 --> 00:39:11.170
Now it is a desecrated lamp.
现在它成了一盏被亵渎的台灯。

963
00:39:11.430 --> 00:39:11.570
Yeah.
对。

964
00:39:12.150 --> 00:39:18.110
That, Jason, those are two of the coolest recognition stories we've heard on the show, certainly.
杰森，那些绝对是我们在节目中听过最酷的被认出来的故事之二。

965
00:39:18.650 --> 00:39:20.790
It happens at least once a week, I would say.
我想说，至少一周发生一次。

966
00:39:20.890 --> 00:39:21.810
It's a strange thing.
这挺奇怪的。

967
00:39:21.970 --> 00:39:23.210
We don't understand.
我们搞不懂。

968
00:39:23.690 --> 00:39:25.550
I mean, no one can game anything.
我的意思是，没人能预知结果。

969
00:39:25.550 --> 00:39:26.470
It's the William Goldman.
正如威廉·戈德曼所说。

970
00:39:26.610 --> 00:39:27.350
No one knows anything.
谁也不知道答案。

971
00:39:27.530 --> 00:39:29.590
But like, you know, we made this show.
但你知道，我们制作了这档节目。

972
00:39:29.590 --> 00:39:30.270
You make every show.
你们制作了每一档节目。

973
00:39:30.330 --> 00:39:30.850
I don't know.
我不知道。

974
00:39:30.950 --> 00:39:32.650
I throw everything I got at everything.
我把所有的心血都倾注在每一件事上。

975
00:39:32.830 --> 00:39:34.030
You know, you're trying your beSt.
你知道的，你已经尽力了。

976
00:39:34.610 --> 00:39:39.130
And some shows, for whatever reason, just have a stickiness and a staying power.
有些节目，不管出于什么原因，就是有着极高的粘性和生命力。

977
00:39:39.470 --> 00:39:41.510
And this one is one of those, you know?
而这部就是其中之一，对吧？

978
00:39:42.030 --> 00:39:44.250
And I think we're minting new fans.
而且我认为我们正在吸引新的粉丝。

979
00:39:44.390 --> 00:39:46.990
You know, I think parents who grew up watching it are now showing it to their kids.
你知道，我认为那些看着它长大的父母现在正把它放给他们的孩子看。

980
00:39:47.070 --> 00:39:51.010
I just think there's, it is not, I am not only approached by Gen X and millennials.
我只是觉得，不仅是X世代和千禧一代来找我。

981
00:39:51.010 --> 00:39:54.010
I am approached by young people, older people.
年轻人、老年人都会来找我。

982
00:39:54.010 --> 00:39:58.590
But like, it is such a wide cross-section of humanity that loves this show.
但是，喜爱这部节目的受众群体跨度真的非常广泛。

983
00:39:58.850 --> 00:40:00.490
Have your kids seen How I Met Your Mother?
你的孩子们看过《老爸老妈浪漫史》吗？

984
00:40:00.490 --> 00:40:01.970
I'm very nervous asking this.
我问这个时心里很紧张。

985
00:40:02.130 --> 00:40:02.810
They clearly haven't.
他们显然没看过。

986
00:40:02.890 --> 00:40:03.470
Because you're in it.
因为你在里面演出了。

987
00:40:03.690 --> 00:40:05.530
That would be watching something their dad is in.
那等于是在看他们老爸演的东西。

988
00:40:05.710 --> 00:40:05.830
Yeah.
对。

989
00:40:06.470 --> 00:40:07.310
I've recommended it.
我推荐过。

990
00:40:07.490 --> 00:40:09.010
I've recommended it to them.
我向他们推荐过。

991
00:40:09.450 --> 00:40:11.610
You've recommended all your body of work to them.
你把你所有的作品都推荐给他们了。

992
00:40:12.210 --> 00:40:14.430
I've got these other shows and How I Met Your Mother was one of them.
我还有其他这些节目，《老爸老妈浪漫史》就是其中之一。

993
00:40:14.550 --> 00:40:15.950
Are they doing it to fuck with you?
他们这么做是为了捉弄你吗？

994
00:40:16.010 --> 00:40:17.150
Is there a chance they know?
有没有可能是他们知道？

995
00:40:17.150 --> 00:40:17.450
Maybe.
也许吧。

996
00:40:17.630 --> 00:40:17.910
Maybe.
也许吧。

997
00:40:17.990 --> 00:40:18.390
I don't know.
我不知道。

998
00:40:18.610 --> 00:40:19.130
You don't even know.
你甚至都不知道。

999
00:40:19.130 --> 00:40:19.990
I don't know.
我不知道。

1000
00:40:20.250 --> 00:40:25.370
Well, if you have a sixth sense when you're a kid of like, how am I going to hurt my parents
好吧，如果你还是个孩子的时候有一种第六感，知道怎么去伤害你的父母的话

1001
00:40:25.370 --> 00:40:26.010
the most?
最多的那个？

1002
00:40:26.210 --> 00:40:26.610
That was it.
就是这样。

1003
00:40:26.830 --> 00:40:27.390
That was it.
就是这样。

1004
00:40:27.810 --> 00:40:27.860
I'm going to deny.
我打算否认。

1005
00:40:28.030 --> 00:40:30.430
I'm not going to watch their classic comedies.
我才不去看他们的经典喜剧。

1006
00:40:30.450 --> 00:40:32.310
I'm not going to feed their narcissism.
我才不会去助长他们的自恋。

1007
00:40:34.110 --> 00:40:34.910
There's enough of that.
那种事已经够多了。

1008
00:40:34.910 --> 00:40:37.730
The one thing they've oriented their whole professional life around, I refuse to give
他们整个职业生涯都在追求的那唯一一件事，我拒绝给

1009
00:40:37.730 --> 00:40:37.950
it to them.
他们。

1010
00:40:38.170 --> 00:40:38.370
Oh my God.
噢，天哪。

1011
00:40:38.950 --> 00:40:41.610
Well, Jason, it's been so good to be with you.
好了，杰森，很高兴能和你在一起。

1012
00:40:41.870 --> 00:40:46.930
We have such fond feelings about you over here at the How We Made Your Mother pod and everyone
我们在“我们是如何制作你的母亲”播客这边对你有着深厚的感情，还有

1013
00:40:46.930 --> 00:40:48.270
who works with you on How I Met Your Mother.
所有在《老爸老妈浪漫史》中与你合作过的人。

1014
00:40:48.270 --> 00:40:49.470
We're so lucky you did the show.
我们有幸你能来演这部剧。

1015
00:40:49.710 --> 00:40:50.510
You were great on it.
你在里面表现得很棒。

1016
00:40:50.610 --> 00:40:53.710
And maybe we'll give you a shout out for that later episode, too, to get your take
或许我们等会儿也会在后面那一集里提到你，听听你对

1017
00:40:53.710 --> 00:40:53.990
on that.
那一集的看法。

1018
00:40:54.130 --> 00:40:57.610
Because that's a great episode where Tony tries to make amends to Ted.
因为那一集太棒了，托尼试图向泰德弥补过失。

1019
00:40:57.910 --> 00:40:58.090
Right.
没错。

1020
00:40:58.530 --> 00:41:00.430
And it's really funny, that one.
而且那一集真的很好笑。

1021
00:41:00.790 --> 00:41:02.870
And you had an outsized impact.
你产生了巨大的影响。

1022
00:41:02.870 --> 00:41:04.330
You were on a handful of episodes.
你只演了区区几集。

1023
00:41:04.590 --> 00:41:07.490
But like I said, even those little quiet moments, I think you made an impact.
但就像我说的，即使是那些微小而安静的时刻，我认为你也产生了影响。

1024
00:41:07.710 --> 00:41:13.070
And I love, this is one of my favorite rewatch episodes we've done because I thought the
我喜欢，这是我们做过的最喜欢的重看剧集之一，因为我认为

1025
00:41:13.070 --> 00:41:14.990
ending is a knockout punch of this.
结局简直是神来之笔。

1026
00:41:14.990 --> 00:41:19.990
We have this great Benji Hughes song called Waiting for an Invitation that scores that whole
我们有一首本吉·休斯的精彩歌曲《等待邀请》，为整个

1027
00:41:20.470 --> 00:41:23.170
reveal, that whole, and it is shocking.
大揭秘、整个过程配乐，而且非常震撼。

1028
00:41:23.290 --> 00:41:25.990
I think the first time you see it, we've steered it so much toward Robin's going to be the
我想第一次看的时候，我们把剧情引导得好像罗宾会成为

1029
00:41:25.990 --> 00:41:26.290
problem.
问题所在。

1030
00:41:26.510 --> 00:41:27.010
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

1031
00:41:27.150 --> 00:41:28.110
That's not the real problem.
那可不是真正的问题。

1032
00:41:28.490 --> 00:41:33.110
And watching everybody come in and comfort Ted and intercut with Tony and Stella literally
看着大家走进来安慰泰德，并穿插着托尼和斯特拉

1033
00:41:33.110 --> 00:41:35.190
sailing away on a boat.
乘船离去的画面。

1034
00:41:35.770 --> 00:41:36.670
It's very moving.
非常感人。

1035
00:41:36.850 --> 00:41:38.870
I found it very poignant and dark and weird.
我觉得既辛酸、黑暗又诡异。

1036
00:41:39.330 --> 00:41:41.350
And again, I think it's what sets the show apart.
再说一次，我认为正是这一点让这部剧脱颖而出。

1037
00:41:41.350 --> 00:41:45.570
So thank you for bringing comedy and bringing good acting moments to the show, too, and making
所以谢谢你为这部剧带来喜剧和精彩的演技时刻，同时也让

1038
00:41:45.570 --> 00:41:46.750
the dramatic part work, too.
戏剧部分同样出彩。

1039
00:41:46.810 --> 00:41:47.230
Thank you for that.
谢谢你。

1040
00:41:47.230 --> 00:41:47.910
Thanks for having me.
谢谢邀请我来。

1041
00:41:48.050 --> 00:41:49.990
Thanks for trusting me with your material.
谢谢你信任我的演绎。

1042
00:41:50.250 --> 00:41:53.110
And it's a mutual experience, man.
这也是相互的，老兄。

1043
00:41:53.190 --> 00:41:55.130
We just wanted to get you on that lamp.
我们只是想让你坐上那盏灯。

1044
00:41:55.330 --> 00:41:55.550
That's right.
没错。

1045
00:42:01.730 --> 00:42:04.570
Craig, let's talk about some more fun things in this episode.
克雷g，让我们来聊聊这一集里更多有趣的事。

1046
00:42:04.670 --> 00:42:05.410
Because there's so...
因为有太多……

1047
00:42:05.410 --> 00:42:08.890
I mean, this episode is incredibly deep and kind of wrenching by the end.
我的意思是，这一集内容极其深刻，到最后甚至有点揪心。

1048
00:42:08.990 --> 00:42:11.250
But there's a lot of good jokes in this episode.
