那里有一位女士，她有点像约会和恋爱关系专家。

1246
00:51:21.170 --> 00:51:23.270
And she was really fun, interesting to talk to.
她人非常有趣，跟她聊天很有意思。

1247
00:51:23.390 --> 00:51:24.290
Jordana knows her a bit.
乔丹娜对她略有了解。

1248
00:51:25.050 --> 00:51:27.950
And she was trying to figure out, like, kind of her second act.
她当时在试图摸索自己的第二人生阶段。

1249
00:51:28.070 --> 00:51:29.490
Like, what's the next phase going to be?
比如，接下来的转型会是怎样的？

1250
00:51:29.590 --> 00:51:34.590
And one of the things she did was she found her 10 closest friends and she gave them a questionnaire.
她做的一件事就是找了她最亲密的10个朋友，给他们发了一份问卷。

1251
00:51:35.050 --> 00:51:37.930
And she said, when do you see me at my most alive?
然后她说，你觉得我什么时候看起来最有生命力？

1252
00:51:38.570 --> 00:51:45.670
Like, she just basically asked her friends, like, I need your view of me because I have too many blind spots.
就好像她基本上问她的朋友们，我需要你们对我的看法，因为我有太多的盲区。

1253
00:51:45.870 --> 00:51:46.250
Right.
没错。

1254
00:51:46.390 --> 00:51:54.290
And it was just a reminder that our friends can often have insight into our character or our path or our destiny in ways that we can't see.
这正是一个提醒，我们的朋友往往能以我们自己看不到的方式，洞察我们的性格、道路或命运。

1255
00:51:54.390 --> 00:51:56.130
It's very hard to see ourselves sometimes.
有时候要看清自己真的很难。

1256
00:51:56.670 --> 00:51:56.790
Yeah.
是啊。

1257
00:51:56.790 --> 00:51:58.770
That's why we need outside counsel.
这就是为什么我们需要外界的军师。

1258
00:51:59.570 --> 00:51:59.750
Yeah.
对。

1259
00:52:00.030 --> 00:52:00.770
Trusted counsel.
值得信赖的军师。

1260
00:52:00.870 --> 00:52:01.790
I love that question.
我太喜欢这个问题了。

1261
00:52:02.030 --> 00:52:03.670
When do you see me at my most alive?
你觉得我什么时候看起来最有生命力？

1262
00:52:04.110 --> 00:52:04.410
Yeah.
对。

1263
00:52:04.410 --> 00:52:11.610
She was kind of able to fashion a mission statement about what she wanted to do next based on this crowdsourcing of information from her friends.
通过向朋友们众包这些信息，她差不多能够为自己接下来想做什么拟定一个使命宣言。

1264
00:52:12.410 --> 00:52:13.230
That's great.
太棒了。

1265
00:52:13.730 --> 00:52:16.650
And that's what Rob, I mean, Ted's friends are right.
这就是罗布，我是说，泰德的朋友们是对的。

1266
00:52:16.990 --> 00:52:22.190
He's forcing something and they all see it and he goes through with it anyway.
他在强求某件事，大家都看出来了，但他还是坚持要把它进行到底。

1267
00:52:22.630 --> 00:52:22.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1268
00:52:22.950 --> 00:52:24.010
And it ends in disaster.
结果以灾难收场。

1269
00:52:24.190 --> 00:52:26.330
And this episode ends with real heartbreak.
而这一集以真正的伤心欲绝结束。

1270
00:52:26.330 --> 00:52:33.350
Like, and that moment, it's so well shot and well done that all of Ted's friends sort of dissolve in in that little montage, right?
比如，那个时刻，镜头拍得和处理得都太好了，泰德所有的朋友都在那个小蒙太奇里淡出了，对吧？

1271
00:52:33.350 --> 00:52:37.290
Ted's on the bed, dissolve in Marshall, dissolve in Lily, dissolve in Barney.
泰德在床上，淡出到马歇尔，淡出到莉莉，淡出到巴尼。

1272
00:52:37.390 --> 00:52:43.450
And even Barney plays this, there's this great moment where Barney looks really stricken for his best friend and puts his hand on Ted's shoulder.
甚至巴尼也演出了这一点，有一个极好的瞬间，巴尼为他的挚友感到非常难过，把手搭在泰德的肩膀上。

1273
00:52:43.690 --> 00:52:46.350
And you play the gravitas of that beautifully, Josh.
乔什，你把那种凝重的分量演得太美妙了。

1274
00:52:46.350 --> 00:52:49.690
Josh, and that I love that song at the end, Benji Hughes, Waiting for an Imitation.
乔什，而且我很喜欢最后的歌，本杰·休斯的《等待模仿》。

1275
00:52:50.050 --> 00:52:51.130
That's just a killer song.
那真是一首杀手级的歌曲。

1276
00:52:51.190 --> 00:52:53.670
I've been listening to that song for the past two days because we watched this episode.
过去两天我一直在听这首歌，因为我们看了这一集。

1277
00:52:53.870 --> 00:52:58.850
I was driving around LA and I heard that on like an indie rock radio station.
我当时在洛杉矶开车，在某个独立摇滚电台听到的。

1278
00:52:59.010 --> 00:53:00.190
These things can't happen anymore.
这种事现在不会发生了。

1279
00:53:00.850 --> 00:53:03.730
It was 103.1 used to be this indie rock radio station.
那是103.1，以前是个独立摇滚电台。

1280
00:53:03.910 --> 00:53:09.070
And I tell you, I got at least a half dozen songs for How Much A Mother Offer listening to that station.
我跟你说，听那个电台，我至少为《老爸老妈浪漫史》找到了六首歌。

1281
00:53:10.450 --> 00:53:12.370
And Iggy Pop would have been on that radio station.
而且伊吉·波普也会在那家电台播放。

1282
00:53:12.370 --> 00:53:18.450
And yeah, so I just, I found the, I found it to be a knockout punch, the ending of that episode.
所以，我觉得这一集的结尾简直是致命一击。

1283
00:53:18.590 --> 00:53:26.670
I just found it, watching that ending, that last couple of minutes, I thought, this is what our show does that other comedies weren't doing.
我只是觉得，看着那个结尾，最后那两分钟，我想，这就是我们的剧能做到而其他喜剧做不到的。

1284
00:53:26.890 --> 00:53:27.650
Wouldn't even go near.
甚至连碰都不敢碰。

1285
00:53:28.490 --> 00:53:32.670
Only Himmium could do this, this ending, these last two minutes of this episode.
只有《老爸老妈浪漫史》才能做出这样的结局，这一集的最后两分钟。

1286
00:53:33.290 --> 00:53:37.630
And there was a lot of funny stuff leading up to it, but this is our move.
前面有很多搞笑的内容，但这才是我们的拿手好戏。

1287
00:53:37.630 --> 00:53:44.150
It felt like we are firing on all cylinders as the show that we are, that only we could be in that moment.
感觉我们火力全开，展现出我们本来的剧集面貌，在那个时刻只有我们能做到。

1288
00:53:44.470 --> 00:53:50.410
You know, Barney clearly doesn't want Ted or anyone to get married, but he also doesn't want his friend to be in pain, you know?
你知道的，巴尼显然不想让泰德或任何人结婚，但他也不想让他的朋友痛苦，你知道吗？

1289
00:53:50.470 --> 00:53:50.990
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

1290
00:53:51.190 --> 00:53:52.430
That's really hard for him.
这对他的确很难。

1291
00:53:52.690 --> 00:53:54.830
I love Barney.
我爱巴尼。

1292
00:53:54.910 --> 00:53:56.430
I know a hopeless cause when I see it.
我一眼就能看出什么是无药可救。

1293
00:53:56.510 --> 00:53:57.570
That's why I don't recycle.
这就是为什么我不回收利用。

1294
00:53:57.870 --> 00:53:59.110
What a dark, brutal joke.
多么黑暗、残酷的笑话。

1295
00:53:59.110 --> 00:54:00.290
What a dark, brutal joke.
多么黑暗、残酷的笑话。

1296
00:54:00.290 --> 00:54:03.930
He's really undercutting Ted's and Marshall's entire lives there.
他那里真的是在贬低泰德和马歇尔的整个人生。

1297
00:54:04.030 --> 00:54:04.650
And the Earth.
还有地球。

1298
00:54:04.650 --> 00:54:09.290
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, he throws the Earth under the bus, throws the Earth under the bus, it's very stressful.
对，对，对，对，他把地球也给坑了，把地球给坑了，这太让人紧张了。

1299
00:54:09.310 --> 00:54:14.550
The beautiful mind imagery of Barney plotting out how to sleep with Robin again.
巴尼密谋如何再次和罗宾上床时，那种《美丽心灵》式的意象。

1300
00:54:15.510 --> 00:54:17.030
Again, very Chris Harris joke.
再次说明，非常克里斯·哈里斯式的笑话。

1301
00:54:17.890 --> 00:54:25.270
You know what was my favorite, probably one of my favorite just written jokes, head under her dress like an old-time photographer.
你知道我最喜欢的、可能是我最喜欢的精妙笑话之一是什么吗？钻进她裙子底下，就像老派摄影师一样。

1302
00:54:25.610 --> 00:54:26.930
An old-time photographer.
老派摄影师。

1303
00:54:27.190 --> 00:54:28.950
I wish, that one really caught my ear too.
我希望是，那个也真的很对我的胃口。

1304
00:54:29.070 --> 00:54:31.910
It's just a beautiful turn of phrase, even though it's about something horrifying.
这真是一种精妙的措辞，尽管它说的是一件极其恐怖的事。

1305
00:54:31.910 --> 00:54:34.730
It puts you, you know exactly, you can see it.
它把你代入进去，你完全懂的，你脑海里能浮现出那个画面。

1306
00:54:34.870 --> 00:54:36.050
I can't tell you who wrote that.
我没法告诉你那是谁写的。

1307
00:54:36.450 --> 00:54:38.870
It might have been Chris, it might have been in the room.
可能是克里斯写的，也可能是大家在房间里讨论出来的。

1308
00:54:39.010 --> 00:54:43.630
It was one of those where I was like, I'm jealous of that joke, even though there's a slight chance it could have been my own.
当时我心里就想，我很嫉妒能写出这个笑话的人，尽管它有微乎其微的可能是出自我自己之手。

1309
00:54:44.110 --> 00:54:45.190
Like, you know what I mean?
就，你知道我的意思吗？

1310
00:54:45.250 --> 00:54:47.930
Like, you almost forget, sometimes someone will remind you, like, you pitched that.
就像，你差点都忘了，有时别人会提醒你，比如，那是你提出来的。

1311
00:54:48.010 --> 00:54:51.390
You go, oh, all right, well, past me, I was having a good day that day.
然后你会说，哦，好吧，过去的我自己，我那天状态真不错。

1312
00:54:51.570 --> 00:54:53.410
But I don't, I don't, that one I don't remember.
但我记不清了，那个我真的记不清了。

1313
00:54:53.590 --> 00:54:54.090
I can't remember.
我想不起来了。

1314
00:54:54.190 --> 00:54:57.230
But whatever, how much a mother of a writer that was, it's an A+.
但不管怎样，不管哪个才华横溢的编剧想出来的，这绝对能拿A+。

1315
00:54:57.230 --> 00:55:02.990
Also, a reward for long-time fans, just a little pop of Zitch Dog, which is so pleasurable.
另外，这也是给老粉丝的一个回馈，突然来了一点“扎奇狗”的梗，太让人开心了。

1316
00:55:03.430 --> 00:55:04.090
Mini Zitch Dog.
迷你“扎奇狗”。

1317
00:55:04.230 --> 00:55:09.410
It's that thing of you're accumulating all the references, and you get to do these moves, like the telepathy.
这就好比你积累了所有的梗，然后你就能使出这些招式，就像心电感应一样。

1318
00:55:09.550 --> 00:55:12.870
It's like you just get this, you're building out your toolkit of moves you can do.
就像你得到了这个，你正在建立自己的招式工具箱，随时可以拿出来用。

1319
00:55:13.230 --> 00:55:13.410
Yeah.
对。

1320
00:55:13.770 --> 00:55:17.730
I mean, any road trip, you can go 500 miles, you can go Zitch Dog.
我的意思是，随便什么公路旅行，你可以开五百英里，你可以玩“扎奇狗”。

1321
00:55:17.930 --> 00:55:20.670
Like, you have these little moves within a different context.
就像，你在不同的语境下也能用这些小招式。

1322
00:55:20.670 --> 00:55:22.970
Yeah, and that's season four, as opposed to season one.
对，那是第四季，跟第一季完全不同。

1323
00:55:24.070 --> 00:55:34.110
You know, there's a really fun thing where they come to this, you know, kind of hippie, crunchy wedding venue, and they all become, they all get disappointed in their own ways.
你知道，有个特别有趣的情节，他们来到这个，你知道的，有点嬉皮士风格的健康婚礼场地，然后他们所有人都变了，每个人都用各自的方式感到失望。

1324
00:55:34.210 --> 00:55:35.810
You know, the food is not what they want to be eating.
你知道，食物不是他们想吃的。

1325
00:55:35.930 --> 00:55:36.850
There's no alcohol.
没有酒精。

1326
00:55:37.310 --> 00:55:39.270
Like, everything is disappointing to them.
总之，每件事都让他们感到失望。

1327
00:55:39.530 --> 00:55:39.710
Yeah.
对。

1328
00:55:40.690 --> 00:55:44.930
Could never get enough of Marshall puns, namaste here any longer than I have to.
马歇尔的谐音梗怎么都听不够：“我才不在这儿‘纳嘛死呆’（多待）一秒钟呢。”

1329
00:55:45.090 --> 00:55:46.510
That is a Chris Harris joke.
那是克里斯·哈里斯的笑话。

1330
00:55:46.510 --> 00:55:51.430
And I remember he went, ah, that's a shitty pun, and I was like, no, no, no, that's glorious.
我记得他当时说，啊，这是个烂透了的谐音梗，而我就觉得，不不不，这太绝了。

1331
00:55:51.750 --> 00:55:55.190
To this day, I tell him how glorious that joke is, and he always downplays it.
直到今天，我还经常跟他说那个笑话有多绝，但他总是轻描淡写地带过。

1332
00:55:55.410 --> 00:55:56.750
Namaste here any longer than I have to.
我才不在这儿“纳嘛死呆”一秒钟呢。

1333
00:55:57.510 --> 00:55:58.310
That's genius.
这简直是天才之作。

1334
00:55:58.610 --> 00:55:58.930
That's so good.
太棒了。

1335
00:55:58.930 --> 00:56:05.990
It's literally the line you need to leave, like, a yoga studio or, like, you know, anything you don't want to be.
这简直就是离开瑜伽馆，或者任何你不想待的地方时，你最需要的一句话。

1336
00:56:05.990 --> 00:56:09.270
I think of that line every time I hear the word namaste.
我每次听到“纳嘛死呆”这个词，都会想起这句话。

1337
00:56:09.590 --> 00:56:13.970
Like, that's been ruined for me forever by Chris Harris, but in the best way possible.
就，这个词已经被克里斯·哈里斯彻底毁在我心里了，但却是以最棒的方式毁掉的。

1338
00:56:14.250 --> 00:56:14.470
Yeah.
对。

1339
00:56:14.470 --> 00:56:19.810
Where did the bartender possibly being the lead singer of the Spin Doctors come from?
那个酒保怎么会突然跟“旋转医生”乐队的主唱扯上关系的？

1340
00:56:19.810 --> 00:56:20.410
I can't remember.
我想不起来了。

1341
00:56:22.690 --> 00:56:26.490
And the joke obviously preceded the casting of the guy, right?
而且这个笑话显然是在选角之前就定好了的吧？

1342
00:56:26.750 --> 00:56:27.490
I think so.
我想是的。

1343
00:56:27.650 --> 00:56:31.630
And then I think we found a guy that was sort of slightly had that vibe, but, yeah.
然后我觉得我们找了一个身上确实有点那种气质的演员，不过，对。

1344
00:56:31.770 --> 00:56:31.910
Yeah.
对。

1345
00:56:32.810 --> 00:56:37.550
Jordana did say in the middle of this episode, I am so happy we're not having a wedding or planning a wedding even.
乔达娜在这集演到中间时确实说过，我好高兴我们不办婚礼，甚至都不用筹备婚礼。

1346
00:56:37.770 --> 00:56:39.390
Like, the stress of that.
就像，那种压力太大了。

1347
00:56:39.690 --> 00:56:42.210
And compressed into four days, it's just, it's insane.
而且压缩在四天里，简直，简直太疯狂了。

1348
00:56:42.210 --> 00:56:44.810
I mean, I like the chyron, like, four minutes later.
我是说，我喜欢那个字幕条，写着“四分钟后”。

1349
00:56:45.030 --> 00:56:46.290
Like, four minutes later.
就像，四分钟后。

1350
00:56:48.050 --> 00:56:48.550
Yeah.
对。

1351
00:56:49.110 --> 00:56:56.190
But I did, I told Jason this, but I remember feeling loose and funny in that Tony-Ted scene.
但我确实说过，我告诉过杰森这事，但我记得在拍托尼和特德那场戏时，我感觉整个人很放松、很好笑。

1352
00:56:56.590 --> 00:57:02.290
And I'm just like, Ted, doing a little karate, and then he gets ambushed.
然后我就像是在说，特德，打了一套短小的空手道，接着他就遭到伏击了。

1353
00:57:02.610 --> 00:57:02.870
Yeah.
对。

1354
00:57:03.050 --> 00:57:03.430
Hilarious.
太搞笑了。

1355
00:57:03.510 --> 00:57:07.250
And another moment I like in that scene is Ted saying, actually, I've nailed her a lot of times.
我在那场戏里还很喜欢另一个瞬间，就是特德说，其实，我跟她有过很多次。

1356
00:57:07.390 --> 00:57:09.110
Why do I always have to correct people?
为什么我总是得纠正别人？

1357
00:57:10.230 --> 00:57:14.510
I also like, hey, hey, hey, let's stop hugging.
我也很喜欢，嘿，嘿，嘿，咱们别抱了。

1358
00:57:14.670 --> 00:57:15.330
Let's stop hugging.
别抱了。

1359
00:57:17.190 --> 00:57:18.650
That is a really good scene.
那真是一场非常棒的戏。

1360
00:57:18.830 --> 00:57:21.210
I was so, I forgot how good this one was.
我太……我都忘了这一集有多好看了。

1361
00:57:21.410 --> 00:57:22.430
I really like this one.
我真的很喜欢这一集。

1362
00:57:22.750 --> 00:57:22.930
Yeah.
对。

1363
00:57:23.210 --> 00:57:24.890
It works on a lot of levels.
它在很多层面都很成功。

1364
00:57:25.090 --> 00:57:25.210
Yeah.
对。

1365
00:57:25.410 --> 00:57:26.650
No exes at our wedding.
我们婚礼上不准有前任。

1366
00:57:26.930 --> 00:57:28.750
To be fair, your ex is here.
公平地说，你前任就在这儿呢。

1367
00:57:29.490 --> 00:57:33.550
After driving the guy, after being in the car for six hours to get the guy there.
开车把那家伙带过来之后，在车上待了六个小时才把那家伙送到地方。

1368
00:57:33.550 --> 00:57:39.190
You know what's a great pop also is alt-history of Ted and Stella's kids, those blonde kids.
你知道还有一个很绝的梗吗，就是特德和斯特拉孩子的平行历史，那些金发小孩。

1369
00:57:39.390 --> 00:57:39.650
Yeah.
对。

1370
00:57:39.970 --> 00:57:40.210
Yeah.
对。

1371
00:57:40.410 --> 00:57:42.970
Again, that's just like another move only our show could do.
话说回来，这也是那种只有咱们剧能玩出来的花样。

1372
00:57:43.090 --> 00:57:47.910
It's so weird, this alternate reality future with children and Sarah Chalk's 20 years older.
太诡异了，这个带着孩子的平行现实未来，而且莎拉·乔克老了20岁。

1373
00:57:48.430 --> 00:57:51.990
It's a, there's a lot in 22 minutes in this episode.
这集里，22分钟的内容可真够丰富的。

1374
00:57:51.990 --> 00:57:55.590
It feels like a two-parter, and it's in one batch of 22 minutes.
感觉就像个上下集，结果全塞在短短22分钟的一集里了。

1375
00:57:55.710 --> 00:58:03.110
It's a really good example of how your superpower, if misdirected or misunderstood, can be your total weakness.
这真是一个极好的例子，说明你的超能力如果用错了方向或者被误解了，可能会彻底变成你的弱点。

1376
00:58:03.110 --> 00:58:10.850
Like, Ted's optimism, his certainty that he can make everything work, is shown to be absolute folly in this episode.
比如，特德的乐观，他坚信自己能把一切都搞定的信念，在本集中被证明是绝对的愚蠢。

1377
00:58:11.050 --> 00:58:11.270
Absolutely.
绝对是。

1378
00:58:11.550 --> 00:58:13.210
It's almost a hubris story.
这几乎是一个傲慢的故事。

1379
00:58:13.450 --> 00:58:16.690
It's almost like a Greek mythology hubris story, this episode.
这集简直就像是一个希腊神话里关于傲慢的故事。

1380
00:58:17.110 --> 00:58:19.670
But you love Ted for having that heart.
但你又会因为特德拥有那样一颗心而爱他。

1381
00:58:20.030 --> 00:58:25.750
It's best, it's hubris with the best intentions, and he just wants to, Robin says it in that scene.
这是最好的，这是怀揣着最好初衷的傲慢，而他只是想……罗宾在那场戏里说出来了。

1382
00:58:26.010 --> 00:58:31.790
Robin, I love that scene between Ted and Robin, because Robin names what Ted's damage is in that scene.
罗宾，我很喜欢特德和罗宾之间的那场戏，因为罗宾在那场戏里指出了特德的心理创伤是什么。

1383
00:58:31.790 --> 00:58:34.010
You're trying to skip to the end of the book.
你想直接跳到书的结尾。

1384
00:58:34.270 --> 00:58:34.650
Yes.
没错。

1385
00:58:34.830 --> 00:58:38.330
And you're skipping a lot of good parts, and not just good parts, necessary parts.
而你跳过了很多精彩的部分，不仅是精彩部分，还有必要的部分。

1386
00:58:38.650 --> 00:58:42.050
You can't have the middle of the story if you skip to the end.
如果你直接跳到结局，你就无法拥有故事的中段。

1387
00:58:42.330 --> 00:58:43.770
This isn't how it goes.
事情可不是这样的。

1388
00:58:44.210 --> 00:58:49.790
And I just thought she was so right, and Ted knew she would, the way you played that scene, beautifully acted.
而且我觉得她说得太对了，特德也知道她会这么说，你演那场戏的方式，演技太棒了。

1389
00:58:50.190 --> 00:58:51.030
He's devastated.
他崩溃了。

1390
00:58:51.250 --> 00:58:52.150
He knows she's right.
他知道她是对的。

1391
00:58:52.310 --> 00:58:59.350
By season four, the audience has so many Ted and Robin iconic scenes in their head.
到了第四季，观众脑海中已经有了太多特德和罗宾的标志性场面。

1392
00:58:59.350 --> 00:59:02.290
You know, there's slutty pumpkin on the roof.
你知道的，屋顶上的荡秋千南瓜头。

1393
00:59:02.690 --> 00:59:05.590
There's, I mean, name them.
还有，我是说，随便举几个。

1394
00:59:05.790 --> 00:59:07.410
You know, I would have stolen you a whole orchestra.
你知道的，我本来可以为你偷来一整支乐队。

1395
00:59:07.530 --> 00:59:08.550
There's so many.
真的有太多了。

1396
00:59:09.370 --> 00:59:19.170
So seeing this thing of Robin just kind of throwing up a flare and saying, buddy, I see what you're doing, and I think you're off here.
所以看到罗宾这种抛出一个信号，说，伙计，我看出你在干什么了，我觉得你这里搞砸了。

1397
00:59:19.810 --> 00:59:27.750
And Ted's breath being taken away because he's, you know, even saying, it's like, it was, we broke up for a year, and it's like, that's not that long.
然后特德倒吸了一口凉气，因为他，你知道的，甚至还在说，这就好像是，我们分手了一年，而这就好像是，那也没多长时间。

1398
00:59:28.050 --> 00:59:28.870
That's not that long.
那没多长时间。

1399
00:59:29.070 --> 00:59:29.310
Yeah.
对。

1400
00:59:29.310 --> 00:59:33.270
She's just telling him the truth, and no one has said it this plainly to him.
她只是在跟他说实话，而且从来没有人这么直白地对他说过。

1401
00:59:33.430 --> 00:59:37.610
And she certainly loves him in that moment and is maybe in love with him.
而且她在那个瞬间确确实实爱着他，或许也爱上了他。

1402
00:59:37.710 --> 00:59:40.370
And the fact that you don't know which makes the scene really interesting.
而你不知道到底是哪一种，这正是这个场景非常有趣的地方。

1403
00:59:40.930 --> 00:59:44.070
And I still don't know which, but I like that uncertainty.
而且我直到现在也不知道是哪种，但我喜欢这种不确定性。

1404
00:59:44.330 --> 00:59:53.330
I have a high school friend who was really stuck on some things, and no one was brave enough to tell him except this other friend who pulled him aside and said,
我有一个高中朋友，他当时在某些事情上非常固执，没有一个人有勇气告诉他，除了另一个把拉到一旁对他说这番话的朋友：

1405
00:59:53.390 --> 00:59:55.430
you've got to do this, and you've got to stop doing this.
你必须这样做，你必须停止这样做。

1406
00:59:55.790 --> 00:59:59.730
And they were, like, they were things that were, like, really delicate, you know?
而且那些事，怎么说呢，都是些非常微妙的事，你知道吗？

1407
01:00:00.210 --> 01:00:06.530
And I always admired my friend telling my other friend this because I was like, he really loved him in that moment.
我一直很佩服我的那个朋友对另一个朋友说这些，因为我觉得，那一刻他是真的爱他。

1408
01:00:06.870 --> 01:00:07.210
Yeah.
对。

1409
01:00:07.330 --> 01:00:08.890
Like, he loved him harder than others.
就像，他爱得比其他人更深沉。

1410
01:00:08.890 --> 01:00:10.190
It's hard, but it's love, yeah.
这很难，但这就是爱，是的。

1411
01:00:10.370 --> 01:00:16.350
You know, like, he was really prepared to risk the friendship to help this guy grow.
你知道，就好像他真的做好了冒着友谊破裂的风险去帮助这个人成长的准备。

1412
01:00:16.710 --> 01:00:17.070
Yeah.
是的。

1413
01:00:17.250 --> 01:00:18.250
That's what that scene was.
那场戏就是这个意思。

1414
01:00:18.330 --> 01:00:19.590
That's why that was a great scene.
这就是那为什么是一场伟大的戏。

1415
01:00:19.790 --> 01:00:23.850
And I love that that scene began with Robin hearing she can't come to the wedding and going, oh, thank God.
而且我特别喜欢那场戏的开场是罗宾听说自己不能去参加婚礼，然后说，哦，谢天谢地。

1416
01:00:24.230 --> 01:00:24.530
Yeah.
对。

1417
01:00:24.950 --> 01:00:26.090
Why am I even here?
我到底为什么还要来这里？

1418
01:00:26.310 --> 01:00:26.710
Why am I here?
我为什么在这里？

1419
01:00:26.710 --> 01:00:30.870
I spent 20 hours getting here wondering why, you know, it's so weird to be here.
我花了20个小时来到这里，一直在想为什么，你知道，在这里感觉太奇怪了。

1420
01:00:30.970 --> 01:00:31.990
It is just a double back.
这真是一个急转弯。

1421
01:00:32.190 --> 01:00:39.570
It is really funny that Barney, it's a great kind of B or C story, the Barney thing of, like, I'm here to sleep with Robin.
巴尼的那个部分真的很有趣，作为B线或C线剧情非常棒，就是巴尼那种“我是来和罗宾上床的”的心态。

1422
01:00:39.810 --> 01:00:41.050
The fact that he sleeps with Robin.
事实上他确实和罗宾睡了。

1423
01:00:41.050 --> 01:00:43.590
This woman comes after me with all she's got, and I have to.
这个女人用尽浑身解数来追我，而我不得不这么做。

1424
01:00:43.590 --> 01:00:45.390
And it's not that woman in the end.
但到头来并不是那个女人。

1425
01:00:45.610 --> 01:00:46.330
It's not even that woman.
甚至都不是那个女人。

1426
01:00:46.430 --> 01:00:46.990
It's not even that woman.
甚至都不是那个女人。

1427
01:00:47.030 --> 01:00:49.470
But he ends up, it looks like he ends up riding the tricycle.
但他到最后，看起来他好像骑上了三人自行车。

1428
01:00:49.650 --> 01:00:55.650
I think that, yeah, it's funny that we never come back to quite name that after all the trouble we went to to highlight the belt.
我觉得，是的，很有趣的是，我们在费了那么大劲去突出那个皮带之后，竟然再也没有回过头来给它明确定名。

1429
01:00:55.650 --> 01:01:02.110
And George also said a phrase that we really love, you know, kind of like, at the end, even though Ted is heartbroken, like,
而且乔治还说了一句我们真的很喜欢的话，你知道，大致意思是，到最后，尽管泰德心碎了，就像是，

1430
01:01:02.230 --> 01:01:06.330
that kind of notion of rejection is God's protection or rejection is the universe's protection.
那种拒绝就是上帝的庇护或者拒绝就是宇宙的庇护的概念。

1431
01:01:06.470 --> 01:01:09.770
Like, if it wasn't meant for you, it's not going to be for you.
就像，如果这不是为你准备的，那就绝不会属于你。

1432
01:01:10.010 --> 01:01:10.210
Yeah.
是的。

1433
01:01:10.210 --> 01:01:11.910
And, of course, narrator Ted knows that.
当然，旁白泰德是知道这一点的。

1434
01:01:12.510 --> 01:01:14.850
Heartbroken Ted on the day doesn't know that.
而在当场心碎的泰德并不知道这一点。

1435
01:01:15.010 --> 01:01:22.710
But I used to think about Ted getting left at the altar as this somewhat, I don't know, like, humiliating or hard thing.
但我以前总觉得泰德被遗弃在婚礼圣坛前是一件有点，怎么说呢，挺屈辱或艰难的事情。

1436
01:01:22.850 --> 01:01:25.470
But watching it now, I'm like, yeah, what did you expect, man?
但现在回看，我只想说，拜托，你指望什么呢，老兄？

1437
01:01:25.470 --> 01:01:27.670
You planned a wedding in four days to a woman.
你在短短四天内就筹办了一场婚礼，而新娘...

1438
01:01:27.850 --> 01:01:28.390
You didn't know that well.
你其实根本没那么了解她。

1439
01:01:28.390 --> 01:01:29.630
Four days, and they never even quite get to the altar.
仅仅四天，而且他们甚至都没真正走到婚礼圣坛前。

1440
01:01:29.810 --> 01:01:29.950
Yeah.
是啊。

1441
01:01:30.130 --> 01:01:36.070
Yeah, they never, they never, it's not like he's standing there waiting and she, it just doesn't, it's, it's, the whole thing gets derailed.
对，他们从来没有，从来没有，这不像是他站在那里等着而她，根本不是这样，整件事彻底脱轨了。

1442
01:01:36.470 --> 01:01:40.670
And, for good reason, and, you know, they weren't, they weren't right for each other.
而且这也是情理之中，你知道的，他们本来就不适合彼此。

1443
01:01:40.810 --> 01:01:45.690
Although, he couldn't become, again, he couldn't become the man he needed to be if he hadn't been with Stella.
尽管如此，如果不是和斯黛拉在一起，他同样无法蜕变成他后来所需要成为的那个男人。

1444
01:01:46.070 --> 01:01:46.230
Yeah.
是的。

1445
01:01:46.490 --> 01:01:48.290
Yeah, and you know he's going to recover from this.
对，而且你知道他会从这件事中恢复过来的。

1446
01:01:48.690 --> 01:01:48.850
Yeah.
是的。

1447
01:01:49.190 --> 01:01:50.630
So, yeah, it's a great one.
所以，没错，这真的是很棒的一集。

1448
01:01:50.850 --> 01:01:54.290
Thank you to Jason Jones for being with us to talk about this one.
感谢杰森·琼斯做客我们的节目来谈论这一集。

1449
01:01:54.390 --> 01:01:55.410
I love this episode.
我太喜欢这一集了。

1450
01:01:55.650 --> 01:01:55.870
Yeah.
对。

1451
01:01:56.090 --> 01:01:58.930
It actually shows you the whole relationship was quick.
这其实说明你们的整段关系进展很快。

1452
01:01:59.050 --> 01:01:59.910
The beginning was quick.
开头进展很快。

1453
01:02:00.090 --> 01:02:01.090
There's a two-minute date.
这是一场两分钟的约会。

1454
01:02:01.230 --> 01:02:01.390
Two-minute date.
两分钟的约会。

1455
01:02:01.390 --> 01:02:02.430
Everything is about compression.
一切都在于压缩。

1456
01:02:02.710 --> 01:02:03.330
It's a two-minute relationship.
这是一段两分钟的关系。

1457
01:02:03.710 --> 01:02:05.030
It's a two-minute relationship.
这是一段两分钟的关系。

1458
01:02:05.450 --> 01:02:05.690
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1459
01:02:05.690 --> 01:02:11.290
But sometimes, you know, when you're, especially when you feel that motor, that life clock ticking.
但有时候，你知道的，当你，特别是当你感觉到那个马达，那个生命的时钟在滴答作响时。

1460
01:02:11.670 --> 01:02:11.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1461
01:02:12.050 --> 01:02:16.350
Sometimes you burn through relationships fairly quickly because you're like, we don't have a lot of time to wait.
有时你会相当快地度过一段段关系，因为你会想，我们没有太多时间等待。

1462
01:02:16.430 --> 01:02:17.590
Like, we got to figure this out.
就像，我们得把这个搞清楚。

1463
01:02:17.690 --> 01:02:19.330
Are we a match or are we not?
我们是天生一对还是不合适？

1464
01:02:19.430 --> 01:02:21.670
And sometimes you have to accelerate things to figure that out.
有时你必须加速事情的进程来弄清楚这一点。

1465
01:02:21.910 --> 01:02:22.710
Yeah, absolutely.
对，完全正确。

1466
01:02:23.650 --> 01:02:25.430
Yeah, it's a great, it's a great Tad episode.
对，这是一集很棒的，这是一集非常棒的泰德单集。

1467
01:02:25.630 --> 01:02:26.590
You were great in this one, Josh.
乔什，你这一集表现得真棒。

1468
01:02:26.790 --> 01:02:29.530
And there's a great one that follows this one up.
接下来还有一集非常精彩的后续。

1469
01:02:29.610 --> 01:02:32.090
It is kind of like a two-parter, this into the next one.
它有点像上下集，这一集和接下来的一集。

1470
01:02:32.090 --> 01:02:36.050
And so, join us next week when we talk about Happily Ever After.
所以，请收听我们下周的节目，我们将探讨《从此幸福快乐》。

